    <string name="help_cards_title">How to use the card table</string>
    <string name="help_cards_button">How to use the card table</string>
    <string name="help_cards_draw_title">Draw</string>
    <string name="help_cards_draw_text">Tap the deck (the face-down pile) to take its top card into your hand.</string>
    <string name="help_cards_shuffle_title">Shuffle</string>
    <string name="help_cards_shuffle_text">Long-press the deck to shuffle it. Long-press the discard pile to shuffle the discard pile.</string>
    <string name="help_cards_discard_title">Discard</string>
    <string name="help_cards_discard_text">Swipe a card in your hand up to discard it, or drag it onto the discard pile. Drag it onto the deck to put it on top of the deck.</string>
    <string name="help_cards_hand_title">The whole hand</string>
    <string name="help_cards_hand_text">Long-press your hand to pick up all of it, then drop it on the deck or on the discard pile: the cards go on top. Let go anywhere else to put the hand back.</string>
    <string name="help_cards_scroll_title">Big hands</string>
    <string name="help_cards_scroll_text">When your hand is too wide for the table, drag it sideways to scroll through the cards; every value stays visible and the newest card scrolls into view.</string>
    <string name="help_cards_take_title">Take back</string>
    <string name="help_cards_take_text">Tap the discard pile to take its top card into your hand.</string>
    <string name="help_cards_return_title">Discard back into the deck</string>
    <string name="help_cards_return_text">Drag the discard pile onto the deck to turn it over on top of the deck. Moving cards never shuffles them: cards, hands and piles dropped on a pile go on top of it. Long-press the deck when you want to shuffle.</string>
    <string name="help_cards_view_title">Look at a card</string>
    <string name="help_cards_view_text">Tap a card in your hand to see it full screen. Tap again to close.</string>
    <string name="help_cards_buttons_title">Buttons</string>
    <string name="help_cards_buttons_text">Prefer buttons? The hand-pointer icon at the top shows buttons for every action. The share icon sends your hand as text or as a picture; the chevron hides the top bar for more room.</string>
    <string name="help_cards_reset_title">Reset and decks</string>
    <string name="help_cards_reset_text">Reset shuffles every card back into the deck. The cards icon at the top left opens the deck list: 36, 52 or 54 cards, your custom decks and uploaded decks. Only the current deck’s table is kept when you close the app.</string>
    <string name="help_decks_title">Decks</string>
    <string name="help_decks_button">About decks</string>
    <string name="help_decks_standard_title">Standard decks</string>
    <string name="help_decks_standard_text">36 cards (6 to Ace), 52 cards, or 54 cards with two jokers. Tap a deck to play with it; a different deck starts freshly shuffled.</string>
    <string name="help_decks_custom_title">Custom decks</string>
    <string name="help_decks_custom_text">Tap New custom deck, name it, and tick the cards to include from the 54-card deck. Jokers come first so they are easy to leave out. Edit or delete it with the icons on its row.</string>
    <string name="help_decks_upload_title">Your own decks</string>
    <string name="help_decks_upload_text">Upload a deck in Settings → Cards: a ZIP with card images (and an optional CSV), or a CSV of card names. Up to 1000 cards.</string>
    <string name="cards_help_intro">A deck can have up to 1000 cards. Upload one of three kinds of file:</string>
    <string name="cards_help_zip_csv_title">1. ZIP with a CSV and images</string>
    <string name="cards_help_zip_csv_text">A .csv file at the top of the ZIP lists the cards in order. Columns: name, value, suit, image. The header row is optional; image is a path inside the ZIP. Cards without an image are drawn as text.</string>
    <string name="cards_help_zip_images_title">2. ZIP of images only</string>
    <string name="cards_help_zip_images_text">One image per card, in file-name order (card2 comes before card10). The card name is the file name: the_tower.png becomes “the tower”.</string>
    <string name="cards_help_csv_title">3. A plain CSV</string>
    <string name="cards_help_csv_text">Just the list of cards (name, value, suit). Every card is drawn as text.</string>
    <string name="cards_help_images_title">Images</string>
    <string name="cards_help_images_text">• PNG, JPG or WebP, portrait 5:7 (for example 500×700 px); larger images are scaled down to 1024 px.\n• Put back.png (or .jpg, .webp) at the top of the ZIP for the card back; without it, the back follows the app theme.\n• Limits: 10 MB per image, 200 MB per ZIP, 1 MB per CSV.</string>
    <string name="cards_help_csv_example" translatable="false">name,value,suit,image\nRam 1,1,Rams,images/rams_01.png\nCrow 13,13,Crows,images/crows_13.png\nRed Joker,Joker,,images/joker_red.png</string>
    <string name="cards_help_zip_tree" translatable="false">my_deck.zip\n├── cards.csv      (optional)\n├── back.png       (optional)\n└── images/\n    ├── rams_01.png\n    └── crows_13.png</string>

