    <string name="pool_help_csv_title">CSV</string>
    <string name="pool_help_csv_text">UTF-8, comma-separated, with standard quoting. The header row name,image,color is optional; without it the columns are read in that order. Only name is required. color is #RRGGBB or #AARRGGBB. A plain CSV ignores the image column.</string>
    <string name="pool_help_csv_example" translatable="false">name,image,color\nApple,images/apple.png,#E53935\nBanana,images/banana.jpg,#FDD835\nCherry,,#8E24AA</string>
    <string name="pool_help_zip_title">ZIP with images</string>
    <string name="pool_help_zip_text">items.csv at the top of the ZIP (one wrapper folder is fine); image paths are relative to the ZIP root.</string>
    <string name="pool_help_zip_tree" translatable="false">pool.zip\n├── items.csv\n└── images/\n    ├── apple.png\n    └── banana.jpg</string>
    <string name="pool_help_rules_title">Rules</string>
    <string name="pool_help_rules_text">• Images: PNG, JPG or WebP, up to 10 MB each; larger than 1024 px is scaled down.\n• A missing or unsupported image: the item is imported without it.\n• A name already in the pool (or earlier in the file) gets “ #2”, “ #3”…\n• Up to 1000 items; a ZIP up to 200 MB and 1000 files.\n• If the file can’t be read, the pool stays unchanged.</string>
